A||||8||Adrift||What color is the starter selenoid wire? (For Alarm Installation)||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-27-2001||09:48 PM||||I need to hook up my starter selenoid wire to a relay to my alarm to have my started disabled whenever the alarm is triggered. I would like to cut into the starter selenoid wire not at the iginiton area but rather in the centre console, where all the wires run. In the info I was given it says that the starter wire is Yellow - I found two yellow wires running through the centre console and neither of them are it (I cut both of them and the car still started fine). In the center console, what color wire should I use to disable the starter selenoid?||||reg||1
Z||000001||clayatandalusia||11-27-2001||10:25 PM||||the one i pinched off of is above the steering coloum ... its yellow and plugs into a white relay ...  you could trace it back it should go back into the console... i think if you were to look from the windshield to the ECM there are two bundle of wires on the left hand side is a large (about 10ga I dont think its 8 ga) thats yellow... that should be the starter<P>hope this helps<P>Clay Brown <P>85' Med Royal Blue 2M4 SE 5 Speed<BR>84' White 2M4 4 Speed<BR>87' Red 2M6 5 Speed<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-28-2001||12:16 AM||||The overwhelming majority of the wires travelling through the center console are 12-14 gauge, incuding the two yellow ones I found. So, just to prevent me from having to cut and re-attach the wrong wires again, the start wire is a 8-10 guage yellow wire? Is it "faded" Yellow or regular yellow?||||reg||1
