Z||000005||Adrift||11-28-2001||11:02 AM||||So is the starter the heavy purple or the heavy yellow? And what color/thickness is the fuel pump wire?<p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||falconhulk||11-28-2001||11:33 AM||||For the fuel pump wire  go to the fuse block.  Look for the fuse for the fuel pump (its marked) Wires run out from the back.  just cut one of the wires going to the fuse and connect following the same directions for starter sol that came with alarm||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||11-28-2001||11:45 AM||||The purple wire and the yellow wire are the starter. They are located under the dash on the steering column. The yellow is from the ignition switch to the neutral safety switch/ clutch switch. The purple wire goes from the saftey switches to the starter. Cutting this will make the starter not spin. BUT if you have a manual trans car it can still be "pop" started. You can do it this way and if the alarm system screws up you can still start the car if need be. NOTE: You can't push start an auto very easily. I think you have to push it faster than 25mph for the trans to turn the engine. <P>The pink wire goes from the ignition switch to the ignition coil and ECM. This will cut power to the coil and ECM so the car will have no spark or fuel.<P>I usually cut the purple for the starter kill then mount a separate switch for the pink. That way you have to have the alarm de-activated AND the switch flipped to start the car. The ignition kill switch can be mounted anywhere and makes it harder for a thief to steal the car. I only use my switch when in a high theft area like a Mall or unfamiliar city street. At work and home it's not needed since it's in a secure lot at work and in the garage at home.<P><BR>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Adrift||11-28-2001||12:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>The purple wire goes from the saftey switches to the starter. Cutting this will make the starter not spin. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Perfect! Thanks for your help<p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
